  "chapter": {
    "number": 59,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(60) For the end, for them that shall yet be changed; for an inscription by David for instruction, when he had burned Mesopotamia of Syria, and Syria Sobal, and Joab had returned and struck in the valley of salt twelve thousand."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God, you have rejected and destroyed us; you have been angry, yet have pitied us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have shaken the earth, and troubled it; heal its breaches, for it has been shaken.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have shown your people hard things: you have made us drink the wine of astonishment.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have given a token to them that fear you, that they might flee from the bow. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "That your beloved ones may be delivered; save with your right hand, and hear me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God has spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, and divide Sicima, and measure out the valley of tents.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Galaad is mine, and Manasse is mine; and Ephraim is the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 107
          },
          {
            "text": "strength of my head;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Judas is my king; Moab is the caldron of my hope; over Idumea will I stretch out my shoe; the Philistines have been subjected to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who will lead me into the fortified city? who will guide me as far a Idumea?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Will not you, O God, who have cast us off? and will not you, O God, go forth with our forces?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Give us help from trouble: for vain is the deliverance of man.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In God will we",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 108
          },
          {
            "text": "do valiantly; and he shall bring to nothing them that harass us.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 107,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, strengthening.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 59,
          "verse": 7
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 108,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. work power.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 59,
          "verse": 12
        }
      }
    ]
